<rml>
<head>
	<!-- The developer console (consolemodule.py ConsoleWindow): a band at
	     the top of the screen with the last 50 lines of output, the newest
	     at the bottom, a field for the command and a handle that resizes the
	     band's height. While the console flag is on, the game window makes
	     the facade nui_console.ConsoleWindow (controller
	     assets/root/nui_console.py); it opens where legacy's opens (the ","
	     key, in debug mode or after the server's ConsoleEnable), and its
	     commands are legacy's own. The output lines are nui-text: file names
	     and game data, shown as written (tags included), never translated.
	     The body takes no focus but its field. Enter runs the command (an
	     empty field closes the console); Escape in the field closes it. The
	     field lets the game's F keys and Alt through and keeps its focus on
	     a press on a legacy window, as legacy's edit line. The document
	     exists only while the console shows (nui_hud.OnDemand). -->
	<title>console</title>
	<link type="text/template" href="../../nui.rtpl"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="console.rcss"/>
</head>
<body id="console" template="nui" class="nui-window console nui-field-passes-hotkeys nui-field-keeps-focus" data-model="console">
	<div id="console-lines" class="console__lines">
		<div class="console__line" data-for="l : lines" data-attr-id="'console-line-' + l.id"><nui-text links="off" data-attr-value="l.text"/></div>
	</div>
	<div class="console__field">
		<input id="console-field" type="text" maxlength="100" class="nui-input console__input"
			data-event-change="submit(ev.value, ev.linebreak)"/>
	</div>
	<nui-resize id="console-resize" class="nui-resize--bottom-right console__resize" edge="bottom-right" target="console"
		min-height="60" data-attr-width="width" data-attr-min-width="width" data-attr-max-width="width" data-attr-height="height"
		data-event-resized="resized(ev.width, ev.height)"/>
</body>
</rml>
